P-K1: no hypothesis: a minimal siphon contains at most one species of each class of species with the same set of consuming reactions (both sides)
P-K2: (H1) side N / (H2) side D: P(dual) refines S iff no twin pair and every element lies in a minimal siphon
P-K2n: no hypothesis (P's latest version of K2): P(dual) refines S iff no twin pair and every element lies in a minimal siphon (preclusters computed by crn.py even when the dual is not consistent)
P-K3a: WF-FC: the dual is WF-FC (Hack)
P-K3b: WF-FC: extreme conservation rays = 0/1 indicators of minimal siphons
P-K3c: WF-FC: extreme flux rays = 0/1 indicators of minimal T-traps (minimal siphons of the dual)
